{"name":"Teatime","hex":"#be9b79","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"teatime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The traditional time, in the late afternoon, for serving tea (the meal).","A social gathering or conversation centered on sharing gossip, rumors, or other personal news."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teatime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tea (meal)","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an umbrella term for several different meals consisting of food sometimes accompanied by tea to drink. The English writer Isabella Beeton, whose books on home economics were widely read in the 19th century, describes meals of various kinds and provides menus for the \"old-fashioned tea\", the \"at-home tea\", the \"family tea\", and the \"high tea\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg/330px-Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_(meal)","wikidata":"Q245009"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/1280px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFloris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg/500px-Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","s